Hello, dear friends! Tomorrow, we will finally release Episode 5 and it means we have one last riddle for you to solve. It’s quite popular and is often used to challenge the players of adventure and horror games like Silent Hill.

It was originally introduced by Albert Einstein, and even today admirers of this particular riddle tend to come up with new variations for it since flexibility is one of its features.  

Look for some paper and pencil (the best option when it comes to space and zero gravity!), and get ready to rumble!  

[img]https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/30616450/ca377514baba330c7949e4729d133c68b232b559.png[/img]

There are five cabins in a row, numbered from left to right, each of a different color and inhabited by people of different nationalities, with different pets, drinks and jobs. You are given the following clues:

• The English person lives in the red cabin;
• The Spaniard owns the dog;
• Coffee is drunk in the green cabin;
• The Frenchman drinks tea;
• The green cabin is immediately to the right of the ivory cabin;
• The Engineer owns snails;
• The Captain lives in the yellow cabin;
• Milk is drunk in cabin #3;
• The Norwegian lives in cabin #1;
• The Radioman lives in the cabin next to the man with the fox;
• The Captain lives next to the cabin where the horse is kept;
• The Doctor drinks orange juice;
• The Navigator is Japanese;
• The Norwegian lives next to the blue cabin;

Someone drinks water, who is it? 
Someone owns a zebra, who is it?
